cff-version: 1.2.0
title: groundlens
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it. Note that performance figures
  published by this project before v3.0.0 have been withdrawn; see
  RETRACTIONS.md before citing any number from an earlier version.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Marin
    given-names: Javier
repository-code: https://github.com/groundlens-dev/groundlens
url: https://groundlens.dev
abstract: >-
  groundlens reports which words in a generated answer its retrieved sources
  least support, pairing each with the closest matching span in the source.
  Numerals are verified by exact value comparison after format normalisation
  rather than by embedding similarity; other words are scored by maximum cosine
  similarity against the source. The answer-level score is the mean of the k
  weakest anchors rather than the mean of all of them. The library reports no
  verdict and ships no threshold.
license: Apache-2.0
version: 3.0.0
date-released: '2026-08-10'
